==Trivia==
*The word "''Prince''" comes from the Latin word "''prīnceps''", meaning first head.
**The Prince is 1 of 20 [[cards]] associated with nobility, with the others being [[Knight]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Royal Giant]], [[Royal Delivery]], [[Tower Princess]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Raging Prince]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Princess]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Spirit Empress]], [[Super Knight]], [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Royal Chef]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], and the [[Little Prince]].
*The Prince is shown to make the practice of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jousting jousting]. Jousting is a medieval and renaissance martial game or hastilude between two combatants either on horse or on foot. The joust became an iconic characteristic of the knight in Romantic medievalism. The participants of a joust on horseback experience close to three and a quarter times their body weight in G-forces when the lances collide with their armour. Originally, it started as the military use of lances by heavy cavalry, but was transformed into a specialized sport during the Late Middle Ages.
**He is 1 of 5 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that have a charge, the others being [[Battle Ram]], Dark Prince, Raging Prince, and [[Ram Rider]].
***The Battle Ram's charge shares the same sound effects as the Prince's, only at a lower pitch.
*The Prince's pony resembles a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shetland_pony Shetland pony], a breed of ponies that has a compact body with short legs and a long mane, and is commonly ridden in horse shows.
*The Prince is one of the first troop cards to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the [[Minions]], [[Archers]], Knight, [[Spear Goblins]], [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], and [[Balloon]].
*The Prince is one of the first troops to be featured in a [[Loading Screens|Loading Screen]], alongside the Knight, Goblins, and Skeletons.
*The Prince is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Bats]], Royal Recruits, [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, Royal Hogs, [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, Witch, P.E.K.K.A, Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], Mega Knight, Ram Rider, [[Miner]], Royal Ghost, [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Prince is one of the first cards to ever receive balance changes since [[Version History#The First Update (11/1/2016)|The First Update]], the others being the [[Mortar]], Witch, and [[Goblin Barrel]]
*The Prince is 1 of 8 troops that can jump over the river, the others being Hog Rider, Royal Hogs, Dark Prince, Raging Prince, Ram Rider, [[Mother Witch|Cursed Hog]], and [[Santa Hog Rider]].
*The Prince has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Prince is 1 of 23 troops that has been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Fire Spirit]], Bats, [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Firecracker]], Rascal Girls, Royal Hogs, [[Heal Spirit]], Elixir Golem, [[Guards]], Balloon, [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, Ram Rider, [[Sparky]], [[Phoenix]], Royal Ghost, Bandit, [[Lumberjack]], Santa Hog Rider, and the [[Monk]].
*The Prince, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Giant, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, and Night Witch, is featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-theater-stickers/id1353823484 Clash Theater]. Also, along with the Archers, Goblins, Skeletons, Barbarians, Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Wizard, Witch, and [[Princess]], he is also featured in the [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-a-rama/id1182384664 Clash-A-Rama] sticker pack.
*The Prince and the Dark Prince are revealed to be brothers according to the balance changes in the [[Version History#Tournaments%20Update%20(4/7/2016)|Tournaments Update]].
*The grill covering the [[Mega Minion]]'s mouth is very similar to the visor on the Prince's helmet.
*The [[Ranked|Champion League]] badge resembles a Prince's helmet.
*In [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters], the [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Pi%C3%B1ata Piñata] resembles a piñata version of the Prince's pony.
*The Prince is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Prince is the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The Prince is the subject of a few [[Emotes]]. His pony is also the subject of an Emote.
**The Prince is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Prince is one of the first troops to be the subject of a Battle Banner item, along with the Mini P.E.K.K.A, Dart Goblin, P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, Mega Knight, [[Super Witch]], and the Golden Knight.
***The [https://clashroyale.fandom.com/wiki/Battle_Banners?file=Headless_Ponyman_Decoration.png Headless Ponyman decoration] is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Headless_Horseman Headless Horseman].
*His range was shown as 2.5 before the [[Version History#May 2016 Update (3/5/16)|May 2016 Update]].
*The description incorrectly mentions that the Prince does double damage with his charge, as at some Levels, he deals 1 more than double.
*If the player collects the free {{Rarity|Epic}} card from the [[Shop]] in Epic Sunday, while being below [[Arenas|Arena]] 6, the {{Rarity|Epic}} card being given to them will always be the Prince.
*Before the Prince's card release, the Prince was supposed to be a {{Rarity|Rare}} card. However, he was changed to an {{Rarity|Epic}} card post-release.
*The Prince can be seen without his helmet in the [https://youtu.be/N0QqNGbpTK0?si=qs4_dS0-uoPB535E&t=377 LOST & CROWNED] video.

